IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `colc-common`

-- Motor Vehicles Act 1959 (SA), ss 37A, 38, 38A, 38AB, 38B, 40, 40A, with the Motor Vehicles Regulations 2010, reg 76(4)-
-- (5), reg 77(3)-(4) and Schedule 1 clauses 1 and 22 -- the seat-neutral core for the car: the reduced registration
-- fee for a pensioner entitlement card holder (and an incapacitated ex-service owner, an owner who has lost the use of
-- the legs, or the carer of such a child), one trailer, what happens on death or sale, paying the balance, the
-- discretionary refund, and the driver's licence fee with the additional fee on ceasing to hold the card.
--
-- ACTORS (the text's own): the owner and the registered owner or registered operator of a vehicle, the parent or legal
-- guardian of a child, the applicant for and holder of a driver's licence, a person who drives a vehicle, the
-- Registrar. The concession holder's questions are in colc-seat.l4.
--
-- "the Registrar is satisfied by such evidence as the Registrar requires" (ss 38, 38A, 38AB, 38B): the answers are
-- given on the facts stated, and each holds if the Registrar is satisfied of them by that evidence.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. Act: s 37A (ss 38-38B do not apply to a heavy vehicle), s 38 (incapacitated ex-service owner),
-- s 38A (pensioner entitlement card holder), s 38AB (one trailer), s 38B (loss of the use of the legs; the parent or
-- guardian of such a child), the common subsections (2) (one vehicle; no other reduced fee) and (3) (one month after
-- death or the end of ownership), s 40 (paying the balance), s 40A (refund at the Registrar's discretion); s 9(1) is
-- cited only to name what follows a void registration. Regulations: reg 77(3) (66.667%), reg 77(4) (50%), reg 76(4)-(5)
-- (the Registrar's notice for the clause 22(3) fee; recovery as a debt), Schedule 1 clause 1 ("level 2 fee") and clause
-- 22 (driver's licence fees).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: every other registration and licence fee; the prescribed registration fee itself (an INPUT: the
-- Regulations' fee scales are not encoded); s 34 (primary producers) and s 37 (outer areas) except as "another
-- provision" under subsection (2)(b); s 41 (misuse of vehicles registered at a reduced fee); s 42 (transfer of a
-- reduced-fee registration); clause 22(6) (the late-renewal administration fee); Part 4 (compulsory third party
-- insurance, used by the victims of crime encoding).
--
-- EDITION. Act: Open Australian Legal Corpus text as at 2024-11-07 (scraped 2025-03-10), deposited at
-- ../../../motor-vehicles-act-1959/registers/source-bundle/motor-vehicles-act-1959.txt. Regulations: corpus text as at
-- 2025-02-20 (scraped 2025-03-10), deposited at
-- ../../../motor-vehicles-regulations-2010/registers/source-bundle/motor-vehicles-regulations-2010.txt.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website (State of South Australia, CC BY 4.0), taken
-- from the Open Australian Legal Corpus (CC BY 4.0); each text is as at the corpus scrape and may be out of date.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Motor Vehicles Act 1959 and Regulations 2010 -- the core`

§§ `ss 37A, 38, 38A, 38B -- the reduced registration fee`

-- s 38(1)(b): "the owner, as a result of service in a naval, military or air force, is totally and permanently
-- incapacitated, or is blind, or has lost a leg or foot, or receives under the laws of the Commonwealth relating to
-- repatriation a pension at the rate for total incapacity, or a pension granted by reason of impairment of the power of
-- locomotion at a rate not less than 70 per cent of the rate for total incapacity". Schedule 1 clause 22(1)(a) (the
-- licence fee) uses a different list: "(i) is totally or permanently incapacitated; or (ii) has lost a leg or foot; or
-- (iii) receives ... a pension at the rate for total incapacity or a pension granted by reason of impairment of their
-- power of locomotion at the rate of not less than 70% of the rate for total incapacity" (finding 17). The repatriation
-- terms are borrowed Commonwealth terms: a FACT.
DECLARE `Result of service` IS ONE OF
    `totally and permanently incapacitated`
    `incapacitated totally or permanently, but not both`
    `blind`
    `has lost a leg or foot`
    `receives a repatriation pension at the rate for total incapacity`
    `receives a pension for impairment of the power of locomotion at 70% or more of the rate for total incapacity`
    `none of these, or no such service`

GIVEN `r` IS A `Result of service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets section 38(1)(b)` `r` IF
        `r` EQUALS `totally and permanently incapacitated`
    OR  `r` EQUALS `blind`
    OR  `r` EQUALS `has lost a leg or foot`
    OR  `r` EQUALS `receives a repatriation pension at the rate for total incapacity`
    OR  `r` EQUALS `receives a pension for impairment of the power of locomotion at 70% or more of the rate for total incapacity`

GIVEN `r` IS A `Result of service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets Schedule 1 clause 22(1)(a)` `r` IF
        `r` EQUALS `totally and permanently incapacitated`
    OR  `r` EQUALS `incapacitated totally or permanently, but not both`
    OR  `r` EQUALS `has lost a leg or foot`
    OR  `r` EQUALS `receives a repatriation pension at the rate for total incapacity`
    OR  `r` EQUALS `receives a pension for impairment of the power of locomotion at 70% or more of the rate for total incapacity`

-- The owner and one motor vehicle, for the period for which registration is sought.
-- s 38A(1)(a): the owner "is entitled, as the holder of a pensioner entitlement card issued under an Act or law of the
-- Commonwealth, to travel on public transport in this State at reduced fares" -- one FACT.
DECLARE `Motor vehicle and owner` HAS
    `the vehicle is a heavy vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner is entitled, as the holder of a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card, to reduced public transport fares in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner has been a member of a naval, military or air force of Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `as a result of that service the owner` IS A `Result of service`
    `the owner, from the loss of the use of 1 or both legs, is permanently unable to use public transport` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner is the parent or legal guardian of a child who, from the loss of the use of 1 or both legs, is permanently unable to use public transport` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the vehicle will be wholly or mainly used for the transport of the owner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the vehicle will be wholly or mainly used for transporting the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another motor vehicle of the owner is already registered at a reduced fee under the same section` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a reduced fee is payable for the vehicle under a provision of the Act other than sections 38 to 38B` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 37A: "Sections 38 to 38B (inclusive) do not apply in relation to a heavy vehicle."
-- s 38(1): "(a) a motor vehicle is owned by a person who has been a member of a naval, military or air force of Her
-- Majesty; and (b) [the result of service]; and (c) the motor vehicle will, during the period for which it is sought to
-- be registered, be wholly or mainly used for the transport of the owner".
GIVEN `v` IS A `Motor vehicle and owner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 38(1) conditions are met` `v` IF
        (NOT (`v`'s `the vehicle is a heavy vehicle`))
    AND `v`'s `the owner has been a member of a naval, military or air force of Her Majesty`
    AND `meets section 38(1)(b)` (`v`'s `as a result of that service the owner`)
    AND `v`'s `the vehicle will be wholly or mainly used for the transport of the owner`

-- s 38A(1): "(a) [the owner] is entitled, as the holder of a pensioner entitlement card issued under an Act or law of the
-- Commonwealth, to travel on public transport in this State at reduced fares; and (b) the motor vehicle will, during
-- the period for which it is sought to be registered, be wholly or mainly used for the transport of the owner".
GIVEN `v` IS A `Motor vehicle and owner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 38A(1) conditions are met` `v` IF
        (NOT (`v`'s `the vehicle is a heavy vehicle`))
    AND `v`'s `the owner is entitled, as the holder of a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card, to reduced public transport fares in this State`
    AND `v`'s `the vehicle will be wholly or mainly used for the transport of the owner`

-- s 38B(1): "(a) that (i) the owner of a motor vehicle, in consequence of the loss of the use of 1 or both legs, is
-- permanently unable to use public transport; and (ii) the motor vehicle will ... be wholly or mainly used for the
-- transport of the owner; or (b) that (i) the owner of a motor vehicle is the parent or legal guardian of a child who,
-- in consequence of the loss by the child of the use of 1 or both of the child's legs, is permanently unable to use
-- public transport; and (ii) the motor vehicle will ... be wholly or mainly used for transporting the child".
GIVEN `v` IS A `Motor vehicle and owner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 38B(1) conditions are met` `v` IF
        (NOT (`v`'s `the vehicle is a heavy vehicle`))
    AND (    (    `v`'s `the owner, from the loss of the use of 1 or both legs, is permanently unable to use public transport`
              AND `v`'s `the vehicle will be wholly or mainly used for the transport of the owner`)
         OR  (    `v`'s `the owner is the parent or legal guardian of a child who, from the loss of the use of 1 or both legs, is permanently unable to use public transport`
              AND `v`'s `the vehicle will be wholly or mainly used for transporting the child`))

GIVEN `v` IS A `Motor vehicle and owner`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`how many of sections 38, 38A and 38B have their conditions met` `v` MEANS
    `one if` (`the section 38(1) conditions are met` `v`)
        PLUS `one if` (`the section 38A(1) conditions are met` `v`)
        PLUS `one if` (`the section 38B(1) conditions are met` `v`)
    WHERE
        GIVEN `b` IS A BOOLEAN
        GIVETH A NUMBER
        `one if` `b` MEANS IF `b` THEN 1 ELSE 0

DECLARE `Why no registration reduction` IS ONE OF
    `the vehicle is a heavy vehicle (section 37A)`
    `the conditions of sections 38, 38A and 38B are not met`
    `another of my vehicles already has the reduced fee under that section (subsection (2)(a))`
    `a reduced fee is payable under another provision of the Act (subsection (2)(b))`

DECLARE `Registration concession` IS ONE OF
    `section 38: the registration fee reduced by 66.667%`
    `section 38A: the registration fee reduced by 50%`
    `section 38B: the registration fee reduced by 50%`
    `no reduction under sections 38 to 38B` HAS `because` IS A `Why no registration reduction`
    `not covered: more than one of sections 38, 38A and 38B would apply, and each excludes a vehicle with a reduced fee under another of them`

-- ss 38(2), 38A(2), 38B(2): "This section does not apply to or in relation to (a) more than one motor vehicle owned by
-- the same owner; or (b) any motor vehicle in respect of the registration of which a reduced fee is payable pursuant to
-- any provision of this Act other than this section." Where two of the three sections would each apply, each one's
-- (2)(b) points at the other, and the text does not say which gives way: `not covered` (finding 16).
GIVEN `v` IS A `Motor vehicle and owner`
GIVETH A `Registration concession`
`the registration concession for the vehicle` `v` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `v`'s `the vehicle is a heavy vehicle`
            THEN `no reduction under sections 38 to 38B` `the vehicle is a heavy vehicle (section 37A)`
        IF `how many of sections 38, 38A and 38B have their conditions met` `v` EQUALS 0
            THEN `no reduction under sections 38 to 38B` `the conditions of sections 38, 38A and 38B are not met`
        IF `v`'s `a reduced fee is payable for the vehicle under a provision of the Act other than sections 38 to 38B`
            THEN `no reduction under sections 38 to 38B` `a reduced fee is payable under another provision of the Act (subsection (2)(b))`
        IF `how many of sections 38, 38A and 38B have their conditions met` `v` GREATER THAN 1
            THEN `not covered: more than one of sections 38, 38A and 38B would apply, and each excludes a vehicle with a reduced fee under another of them`
        IF `v`'s `another motor vehicle of the owner is already registered at a reduced fee under the same section`
            THEN `no reduction under sections 38 to 38B` `another of my vehicles already has the reduced fee under that section (subsection (2)(a))`
        IF `the section 38(1) conditions are met` `v`
            THEN `section 38: the registration fee reduced by 66.667%`
        IF `the section 38A(1) conditions are met` `v`
            THEN `section 38A: the registration fee reduced by 50%`
        OTHERWISE `section 38B: the registration fee reduced by 50%`

§§ `reg 77(3), (4) -- the prescribed amounts`

-- reg 77(3): "For the purposes of section 38(1) of the Act, the prescribed amount is 66.667% of the prescribed
-- registration fee." (4): "For the purposes of sections 38A(1), 38AB(1) and 38B(1) of the Act, the prescribed amount is
-- 50% of the prescribed registration fee." The prescribed registration fee is an INPUT. No rounding is stated.
GIVEN `c` IS A `Registration concession`, `the prescribed registration fee` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the prescribed amount of the reduction` `c` `the prescribed registration fee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `c`
    WHEN `section 38: the registration fee reduced by 66.667%` THEN `the prescribed registration fee` TIMES 66.667%
    WHEN `section 38A: the registration fee reduced by 50%` THEN `the prescribed registration fee` TIMES 50%
    WHEN `section 38B: the registration fee reduced by 50%` THEN `the prescribed registration fee` TIMES 50%
    OTHERWISE 0

-- "the prescribed registration fee for that motor vehicle must be reduced by the prescribed amount".
GIVEN `c` IS A `Registration concession`, `the prescribed registration fee` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the registration fee after the reduction` `c` `the prescribed registration fee` MEANS
    `the prescribed registration fee` MINUS `the prescribed amount of the reduction` `c` `the prescribed registration fee`

§§ `s 38AB -- one trailer`

DECLARE `Trailer and owner` HAS
    `the trailer is a heavy vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner is entitled, as the holder of a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card, to reduced public transport fares in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trailer will be wholly or mainly employed in the personal use of the owner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another trailer of the owner is already registered at a reduced fee under section 38AB` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 38AB(1): "(a) [the owner of a trailer] is entitled, as the holder of a pensioner entitlement card issued under an
-- Act or law of the Commonwealth, to travel on public transport in this State at reduced fares; and (b) the trailer
-- will, during the period for which it is sought to be registered, be wholly or mainly employed in the personal use of
-- the owner, the prescribed registration fee for that trailer must be reduced by the prescribed amount." (2): "This
-- section does not authorise the registration at a reduced fee of more than one trailer owned by the same owner."
-- s 37A applies (s 38AB lies between ss 38 and 38B). s 38AB has no subsection like (2)(b).
GIVEN `t` IS A `Trailer and owner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trailer's registration fee is reduced under section 38AB` `t` IF
        (NOT (`t`'s `the trailer is a heavy vehicle`))
    AND `t`'s `the owner is entitled, as the holder of a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card, to reduced public transport fares in this State`
    AND `t`'s `the trailer will be wholly or mainly employed in the personal use of the owner`
    AND (NOT (`t`'s `another trailer of the owner is already registered at a reduced fee under section 38AB`))

GIVEN `t` IS A `Trailer and owner`, `the prescribed registration fee` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the trailer's registration fee after the reduction` `t` `the prescribed registration fee` MEANS
    IF `the trailer's registration fee is reduced under section 38AB` `t`
    THEN `the prescribed registration fee` MINUS (`the prescribed registration fee` TIMES 50%)
    ELSE `the prescribed registration fee`

§§ `ss 38(3), 38A(3), 38AB(3), 38B(3), 40, 40A -- death, sale, the balance and refunds`

DECLARE `Event during a reduced-fee registration` IS ONE OF
    `the registered owner dies`
    `the registered owner ceases to be the owner of the vehicle`
    `the owner stops holding the card or ceases to meet the conditions, still owning the vehicle`
    `nothing changes`

-- s 38A(3): "If the registered owner of a motor vehicle that has been registered at a reduced fee in accordance with
-- this section dies, or ceases to be the owner of the vehicle, the registration will, subject to this Act, continue in
-- force for a period of one month after death, or the cessation of ownership, and will, unless the balance of the
-- prescribed registration fee is paid, become void on the expiration of that period." ss 38(3), 38AB(3), 38B(3) say the
-- same. Nothing in these sections reaches an owner who keeps the vehicle but stops holding the card (finding 18).
GIVEN `e` IS AN `Event during a reduced-fee registration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsection (3) applies to the event` `e` IF
        `e` EQUALS `the registered owner dies`
    OR  `e` EQUALS `the registered owner ceases to be the owner of the vehicle`

-- The last day of the month in which the registration continues (READING of "one month after": `one month after` in
-- colc-common.l4).
GIVEN `the day of death or the end of ownership` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the reduced-fee registration becomes void unless the balance is paid` `the day of death or the end of ownership` MEANS
    `one month after` `the day of death or the end of ownership`

-- s 40: "Where a vehicle has been registered at a reduced registration fee, the registered owner or the registered
-- operator of the vehicle may, at any time while that registration is in force, pay to the Registrar the balance of the
-- prescribed registration fee, and thereafter during the balance of the period for which it was registered, the
-- vehicle may be used as if it had been registered upon payment of the prescribed registration fee."
GIVEN `the prescribed registration fee` IS A NUMBER, `the reduced fee paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the balance of the prescribed registration fee` `the prescribed registration fee` `the reduced fee paid` MEANS
    `the prescribed registration fee` MINUS `the reduced fee paid`

-- s 40A: "Where a vehicle has been registered upon payment of the prescribed registration fee and the owner of the
-- vehicle becomes entitled to an exemption from, or reduction of, registration fees at any time during the period for
-- which the vehicle is registered, the Registrar has a discretion to refund to the owner of the vehicle such part of the
-- registration fee as the Registrar thinks just in the circumstances." The amount is the Registrar's: answered
-- conditionally.
DECLARE `Refund on becoming entitled` IS ONE OF
    `the Registrar may refund such part of the registration fee as the Registrar thinks just`
    `no refund under section 40A`

GIVEN `registered on payment of the prescribed registration fee` IS A BOOLEAN, `became entitled to a reduction during the registration period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Refund on becoming entitled`
`the section 40A refund` `registered on payment of the prescribed registration fee` `became entitled to a reduction during the registration period` MEANS
    IF `registered on payment of the prescribed registration fee` AND `became entitled to a reduction during the registration period`
    THEN `the Registrar may refund such part of the registration fee as the Registrar thinks just`
    ELSE `no refund under section 40A`

§§ `Schedule 1 clauses 1, 22 -- the driver's licence fee`

-- cl 22(7): "pensioner entitlement card holder means a person who (a) holds a pensioner entitlement card issued under an
-- Act or law of the Commonwealth; and (b) is entitled, as the holder of such a card, to travel on public transport in
-- this State at reduced fares".
DECLARE `Licence applicant` HAS
    `as a result of service in a naval, military or air force of His Majesty the applicant` IS A `Result of service`
    `the applicant is a pensioner entitlement card holder` IS A BOOLEAN

-- cl 22(1): "For the issue or renewal of a driver's licence (a) where the applicant is a person who as a result of
-- their service ... [the clause 22(1)(a) list] (per year) $26.00; (b) where the applicant is a pensioner entitlement
-- card holder (per year) $26.00; (c) in any other case (per year) $53.00".
`the clause 22(1)(a) and (b) annual fee` MEANS 26
`the clause 22(1)(c) annual fee` MEANS 53

GIVEN `a` IS A `Licence applicant`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the annual driver's licence fee` `a` MEANS
    IF     `meets Schedule 1 clause 22(1)(a)` (`a`'s `as a result of service in a naval, military or air force of His Majesty the applicant`)
        OR `a`'s `the applicant is a pensioner entitlement card holder`
    THEN `the clause 22(1)(a) and (b) annual fee`
    ELSE `the clause 22(1)(c) annual fee`

-- cl 22(3)(d): "the annual fee that would have been payable for the issue or renewal of the licence if the person had
-- not been a pensioner entitlement card holder".
GIVEN `a` IS A `Licence applicant`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the annual driver's licence fee without the card` `a` MEANS
    IF `meets Schedule 1 clause 22(1)(a)` (`a`'s `as a result of service in a naval, military or air force of His Majesty the applicant`)
    THEN `the clause 22(1)(a) and (b) annual fee`
    ELSE `the clause 22(1)(c) annual fee`

-- cl 22(2): "The licence fee for a driver's licence issued or renewed for a period other than for full years is 1
-- quarter of the annual licence fee for each complete 3 months of the period for which the licence is issued or
-- renewed." A full year is four complete 3-month periods, so one rule serves both.
GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of complete 3 month periods in` `months` MEANS
    FLOOR (`months` DIVIDED BY 3)

GIVEN `a` IS A `Licence applicant`, `the months of the licence period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the driver's licence fee for the period` `a` `the months of the licence period` MEANS
    `the number of complete 3 month periods in` `the months of the licence period` TIMES (`the annual driver's licence fee` `a` DIVIDED BY 4)

-- cl 22(5): "Administration fee (payable in addition to the licence fee) for the issue or renewal of a driver's licence:
-- level 2 fee"; cl 1: "level 2 fee means an administration fee of $20.00".
`the level 2 fee` MEANS 20
`the administration fee for the issue or renewal of a driver's licence` MEANS `the level 2 fee`

-- cl 22(3): "If (a) a person ceases to be a pensioner entitlement card holder; and (b) the person holds a driver's
-- licence that was issued or renewed on payment of a reduced fee, the person must pay an additional fee of an amount
-- that is equal to the difference between (c) the amount obtained by multiplying the number of complete 3 month periods
-- in the unexpired period of the licence by 1 quarter of the annual fee paid for the issue or renewal of the licence;
-- and (d) the amount obtained by multiplying the number of complete 3 month periods in the unexpired period of the
-- licence by 1 quarter of the annual fee that would have been payable ... if the person had not been a pensioner
-- entitlement card holder." (4): "the unexpired period of the licence commences on the day on which the person ceases
-- to be a pensioner entitlement card holder." READING: the unexpired period runs to the end of the licence's expiry day,
-- and a 3 month period is three calendar months (finding 19).
GIVEN `the day the person ceases to be a card holder` IS A DATE, `the licence's expiry day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the complete 3 month periods in the unexpired period of the licence` `the day the person ceases to be a card holder` `the licence's expiry day` MEANS
    `the number of complete 3 month periods in` (`complete months from` `the day the person ceases to be a card holder` `to the start of` (`the day after` `the licence's expiry day`))

GIVEN `a` IS A `Licence applicant`, `issued or renewed on payment of a reduced fee` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day the person ceases to be a card holder` IS A DATE, `the licence's expiry day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the additional licence fee on ceasing to be a card holder` `a` `issued or renewed on payment of a reduced fee` `the day the person ceases to be a card holder` `the licence's expiry day` MEANS
    IF `issued or renewed on payment of a reduced fee`
    THEN `quarters` TIMES ((`the annual driver's licence fee without the card` `a` MINUS `the clause 22(1)(a) and (b) annual fee`) DIVIDED BY 4)
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `quarters` MEANS `the complete 3 month periods in the unexpired period of the licence` `the day the person ceases to be a card holder` `the licence's expiry day`

-- reg 76(4): "The Registrar may, by written notice given to a person who is liable to pay the fee prescribed by clause
-- 22(3) of Schedule 1, require the person to pay the fee within the time specified in the notice (being a period of not
-- less than 14 days from the day on which the notice is given)."
`the least number of days the Registrar's notice must allow` MEANS 14

GIVEN `the days the notice allows` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar's notice allows enough time` `the days the notice allows` IF
    `the days the notice allows` AT LEAST `the least number of days the Registrar's notice must allow`

§§ `Regulative rules -- the owner, the driver and the licence holder`

DECLARE `Vehicle party` IS ONE OF
    `the registered owner or operator`
    `a person driving the vehicle`
    `the licence holder`
    `the Registrar`

DECLARE `Vehicle act` IS ONE OF
    `pay the Registrar the balance of the prescribed registration fee` HAS `the balance paid` IS A NUMBER
    `drive the vehicle, or cause it to stand, on a road`
    `pay the Registrar the additional licence fee` HAS `the fee paid` IS A NUMBER

-- s 38A(3) (and ss 38(3), 38AB(3), 38B(3)): after the owner's death or the end of ownership, the registration continues
-- for one month and becomes void unless the balance is paid. s 40 names who may pay: "the registered owner or the
-- registered operator" (after a death, READING: whoever acts for the registered owner). Paying is a choice, not a
-- duty, so not paying is no breach; it makes the registration void, and then s 9(1) applies: "A person must not drive
-- an unregistered motor vehicle, or cause an unregistered motor vehicle to stand, on a road. Maximum penalty: $7 500."
-- Clock: days from the death or the end of ownership.
GIVEN `the balance` IS A NUMBER, `the days in the month that follows` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Vehicle party` `Vehicle act`
DECIDE `s 38A(3) -- after death or sale, pay the balance within one month or the registration is void` `the balance` `the days in the month that follows` IS
    PARTY `the registered owner or operator`
    DO    `pay the Registrar the balance of the prescribed registration fee` (EXACTLY `the balance`)
    WITHIN `the days in the month that follows`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  PARTY `a person driving the vehicle`
          SHANT `drive the vehicle, or cause it to stand, on a road`
          LEST  BREACH BY `a person driving the vehicle` BECAUSE "s 38A(3): the reduced-fee registration became void one month after the owner's death or the end of ownership, the balance unpaid; s 9(1): a person must not drive an unregistered motor vehicle, or cause it to stand, on a road (maximum penalty $7 500)"

-- s 40: the registered owner or operator "may, at any time while that registration is in force, pay to the Registrar
-- the balance". Clock: days from now to the end of the registration period.
GIVEN `the balance` IS A NUMBER, `the days left in the registration` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Vehicle party` `Vehicle act`
DECIDE `s 40 -- the owner may pay the balance while the registration is in force` `the balance` `the days left in the registration` IS
    PARTY `the registered owner or operator`
    MAY   `pay the Registrar the balance of the prescribed registration fee` (EXACTLY `the balance`)
    WITHIN `the days left in the registration`

-- Schedule 1 clause 22(3): the person "must pay an additional fee"; reg 76(4): within the time in the Registrar's
-- written notice (at least 14 days); reg 76(5): "If a fee is not paid as required by a notice given under subregulation
-- (4), the Registrar may recover the fee in a court of competent jurisdiction as a debt due to the Registrar."
-- Clock: days from the day the notice is given.
GIVEN `the additional fee` IS A NUMBER, `the days the notice allows` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Vehicle party` `Vehicle act`
DECIDE `Sch 1 cl 22(3), reg 76(4) -- pay the additional licence fee within the time in the Registrar's notice` `the additional fee` `the days the notice allows` IS
    PARTY `the licence holder`
    MUST  `pay the Registrar the additional licence fee` (EXACTLY `the additional fee`)
    WITHIN `the days the notice allows`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the licence holder` BECAUSE "Sch 1 cl 22(3), reg 76(4): a licence holder who ceases to be a pensioner entitlement card holder must pay the additional fee within the time in the Registrar's notice (at least 14 days); reg 76(5): the Registrar may recover it in a court as a debt"
